  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Verizon Business Network Services obligated $407M in federal contract obligations during FY2026 to date. Verizon Business Network Services performed under 376 awards with an average award size of $1.1M, and obligations were down 6.6% year over year. Department of Defense accounted for $115M of obligations, Department of Health and Human Services accounted for $101M, and Department of Justice accounted for $61.1M. The FY trend shows obligations of $265M in FY21, $496M in FY22, $380M in FY23, $459M in FY24, $436M in FY25, and $407M in FY26. Verizon Business Network Services is concentrated in telecommunications markets. Wired Telecommunications Carriers appears with $353M, Wireless Telecommunications Carriers (except Satellite) appears with $28.8M, and Telecommunications Resellers appears with $10.1M. The FY2026 to date totals are partial because the fiscal year is ongoing. Use the agency and market breakdowns to prioritize capture and compliance work where federal demand and historical obligations are largest.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which federal agencies buy most from Verizon Business Network Services?",
        "body": "Department of Defense is the largest buyer with $115M in obligations. Department of Health and Human Services follows with $101M, and Department of Justice follows with $61.1M. Social Security Administration, Department of the Treasury, and Department of Commerce also appear among the top buyers with $29.6M, $27.4M, and $16.1M respectively."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets and NAICS sectors capture Verizon Business Network Services revenue?",
        "body": "Wired Telecommunications Carriers is the dominant market with $353M in obligations. Wireless Telecommunications Carriers (except Satellite) accounts for $28.8M, and Telecommunications Resellers accounts for $10.1M. Smaller shares appear in Other Computer Related Services and several niche NAICS categories."
      }
    ]
  },
